     2,
     "<div><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div></div><div>I thought about the lavtestLRT.mi function but could not figure it out.</div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div>Did you run the help-page examples?  It works the same way that lavTestLRT() does for normal lavaan objects.</div><div><br></div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\">Terrence D. Jorgensen </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\">   (he, him, his)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\"><br>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics<br>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam<br><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" title=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"text-decoration-line:underline;color:rgb(0,120,215)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792415914109000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26Rf-yY9kkq29e2ObGojb1\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5,99,193)\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</span></a></span><br><div> </div></div>"
    ]
